  "key_observations_html": "<aside class=\"crypto-story-callout\" aria-labelledby=\"key-obs-callout-title\"><p class=\"crypto-story-callout__title\" role=\"heading\" aria-level=\"3\" id=\"key-obs-callout-title\">Key observations</p><ul class=\"crypto-story-callout__list\"><li><strong>TMMF printed metrics were roughly flat this week:</strong> Distributed value near $13.23B (+1.2% 30D) leaves tokenized-cash balances largely range-bound\u2014the market story this week is more about issuer and distribution news than a shift in AUM. Related: <a href=\"https://decrypt.co/376422/franklin-templetons-tokenized-treasury-fund-lands-on-hashkey\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Franklin Templeton&#x27;s Tokenized Treasury Fund Lands on HashKey</a> (Decrypt).</li><li><strong>A global regulatory arbitrage map is emerging:</strong> distributed value clusters into distinct compliance regimes\u2014<strong>U.S. Reg D</strong> ~40% of population AUM (e.g. BUIDL, iBENJI); <strong>U.S. Reg S</strong> ~38% of population AUM (e.g. USYC, USDY); <strong>U.S. mutual fund (N-1A)</strong> ~8% of population AUM (e.g. WTGXX). Issuers appear to anchor products in familiar safe harbors rather than one global standard. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/08/27/blackrock-s-mitchnick-says-macro-case-for-bitcoin-is-strengthening-after-record-trading-in-positive-week\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">BlackRock&#x27;s Mitchnick says macro case for bitcoin is strengthening after record trading in positive week</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Multi-chain footprints are a distribution signal:</strong> Funds listing many networks with thin holder counts usually signal jurisdictional or distribution reach, not deep secondary liquidity on every chain. Related: <a href=\"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMizAFBVV95cUxPM1phN2dFa2NFUXRIbjdFa1l6Y0h3eXhMeEhva1ZfTy1LQWNWRGFpai1KQm9YUjktR3NEaDU3b19fOGdBZ1UtU1ZGTHhXSE9md0tFN1RkVl9sX2QxdUt1Mk1PX1hyQTBEbXJFMThIOVUxSjZpbS1TdFRRSDhTTFlrVnVfWlFkWnFISjVsU20xek9uSWZ6Vm51d3hFVVl4NDM5MW5MTERfWWRmTzBBWm96R05OaWdRWnkwd2ZlV2UzdXhlTlQ0ZmVkc0dMd0k?oc=5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">KiiChain Integrates TRON to Expand 24/7 On-Chain FX and Stablecoin Payments</a> (The Block).</li><li><strong>Rates still matter as much as product and chain choice:</strong> Rate and money-market moves can reshape fund-level inflows as quickly as any chain or product launch story. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/news-analysis/2026/08/26/sec-resurrecting-u-s-crypto-custody-rule-the-previous-administration-failed-to-land\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SEC resurrecting U.S. crypto custody rule the previous administration failed to land</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Issuer strategies are splitting into two models:</strong> <em>Institutional cash rail</em> programs (low holder counts, large AUM per holder\u2014e.g. USYC, BUIDL, iBENJI, USTB) vs <em>global yield / distribution</em> products (broader holder bases, retail- or UCITS-friendly framing\u2014e.g. USDY, WTGXX, BENJI, USTBL). These behave like different businesses under the same \"tokenized MMF\" label. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-crypto-custody-rules-investment-firms-white-house?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SEC sends crypto custody rule overhaul to White House for review</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li></ul><p class=\"crypto-story-callout__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Observations rank fund-level and network aggregates on this page against recent tokenization and money-market headlines. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></aside><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
